        "body": "AppLovin Corp is a public company headquartered in Palo Alto, California, and trades under the ticker APP. It is registered with the SEC under CIK 0001751008. Its website describes AppLovin as an advertising platform for mobile games, saying it reaches over a billion daily users in mobile games and helps consumer brands and gaming apps scale their business profitably. The site lists jewelry, furniture, fitness subscriptions, and word games among the kinds of businesses it serves, and says its ads run fullscreen during natural pauses in the game experience or are chosen in exchange for rewards.\n\nThe site names consumer brands, gaming apps, and agencies as its audiences, and points to a dashboard, a Shopify app, a pixel helper, and a strategy call as entry points. It also links to policy pages covering terms of use, publisher policies, demand partner policies, platform enforcement, privacy, and privacy choices.\n\nThe company's record shows no tracked products, no MCP servers, and no lawsuits. It carries law exposure in California, with a count of 282.",
